Administrative Profile- Previously part of the composite Medak district and Jinnaram mandal, Gummadidala became an independent mandal within the Sangareddy revenue division during the state''s administrative re-districting in 2016


Geography- Gummadidala is a mandal in the Sangareddy district of Telangana, India, defined by key geographic features including its exact coordinates of 17.683°N 78.37°E, a total area of about 113.04 square kilometers, and a flat Deccan Plateau terrain


Gummadidala has a tropical climate with hot summers, mild winters, and a central rainy monsoon season. Current conditions show a temperature of 29°C with partly sunny skies and 60% humidity.
Gummadidala is a mandal and village in the Sangareddy district of Telangana, India, with a total village population of 8,032, a sex ratio of roughly 976 females per 1,000 males, and an overall literacy rate of about 68.79%


Gummadidala''s economy is a developing mix of agriculture, local real estate, and expanding industrial/commercial activity tied to the outer growth of the Hyderabad metropolitan region in Sangareddy district


Tourist Attractions - Gummadidala and its surrounding areas feature local religious sites and historic spots, headlined by the local Step Well, Shree Kalyana Venkateshwara Temple, and the nearby Bonthapalli Veerabhadra Swamy Temple.


Gummadidala future development plans focus on industrial clusters, regional connectivity, and local infrastructure enhancements. Key initiatives include proposed TGIIC industrial park layouts, local civic infrastructure upgrades, and rising residential property layouts.


